# Public keys trusted for git SSH signature verification on this machine,
# consumed through `gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile`.
#
# Without this file configured, `git log --format=%G?` renders N on every
# ssh-signed commit and prints "gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile needs to be
# configured and exist for ssh signature verification" -- so the agent commit
# signatures the docket-run contract mandates were unfalsifiable to every auditor
# on this machine: shadow, the operator, CI, a tribunal seat.
#
# Every entry here is a PUBLIC key; nothing secret lives in this file.
# `namespaces="git"` scopes each key to git's own signing namespace, so
# neither is trusted for ssh-keygen signatures made outside git.

